  "result": "`median()` is added in `src/cli/median.ts` and committed as `7300846`. `npm run fast` passes: biome, boundaries, tsc and 18 related tests.\n\n- **Behavior:** it throws a `RangeError` on an empty list. It sorts a copy, so the input isn't mutated. For an even-length list it returns the mean of the two middle values.\n- **Tests:** `test/cli/median.test.ts` covers a single value, odd length, even length, no mutation of the input, and the empty-list rejection.\n- **Extra change:** a repo rule test requires every test file to have a shard weight. I added `'test/cli/median.test.ts': 0.1` to `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`. The 0.1 is a guess (I copied the value of a similar small test), not a measured figure.\n- **Plan:** it's in `docs/notes/median-plan.md`, with every step ticked off.\n\nI ran only `npm run fast`, not the full `npm run gate`. I didn't push.",
